---
title: Pork and cabbage dumplings
servings: 6
yield: about 6 dozen dumplings
tags: [chinese, pork, lunar new year]
cuisine: chinese
time: 35 minutes
source: Easiest Pork and Cabbage Potstickers Recipe Ever by The Woks of Life, https://thewoksoflife.com/easiest-pork-and-cabbage-potstickers-ever/ ; sauce from The Perfect Dumpling Sauce Recipe by The Woks of Life, https://thewoksoflife.com/dumpling-sauce-recipe/
---

== Filling ==

In a #food processor{}, pulse the @napa cabbage{3%cup}(shredded),
@ground pork{8%oz} and @scallions{1/2%cup}(or leeks) until very fine. Tip it
into a bowl.

Beat the @eggs{1} and set a tablespoon aside for sealing. Add the rest to the
bowl with the @sesame oil{1%tbsp}, @soy sauce{1%tsp}, @salt{3/4%tsp},
@granulated sugar{1/4%tsp} and @ground white pepper{1/8%tsp}. Stir until well
mixed.

== Dumplings ==

Put 2 to 3 tsp of filling in the middle of each of the
@dumpling wrappers{1}(1 pack, round yellow egg). Fold in half and pinch the top
shut with a dab of the saved egg, leaving the sides open.

Heat the @vegetable oil{2%tbsp} in a #nonstick pan{} over medium heat and add
the dumplings. When they sizzle, pour in @water{1/4%cup} and cover at once.
Cook ~{3%minutes}, until the water is gone, adding a splash more if needed.

Uncover and cook ~{1%minute} to 2 minutes more, until the bottoms are crisp.
Turn them out onto a plate, crisp side up.

== Dipping sauce ==

Dissolve the @granulated sugar{1%tsp} in @water{1%tbsp}(hot). Stir in the
@soy sauce{2%tbsp}, @rice vinegar{1%tsp}, @chili oil{1%tsp},
@garlic{1%tsp}(minced), @toasted sesame seeds{1%tsp} and
@sesame oil{1/2%tsp}. Serve alongside.

> Use yellow egg wrappers rather than the white kind; they brown better.
